  "EditorMetadata": {
    "Description": "P1b/GAP-12 proof (GAP-1, Hill-attack -\u003E Blueprints slice 4): Condition_AreAllAtBaseline rebuilt as a visually-authored AiPrimitive BTreeCondition, exercising the in-body Branch -\u003E inline if/else scheduler path together with P2 (foreign-entity component read), P1a (FlowForEach loop), and the native Compare node (GAP-12). Graph: init WorkingState bool AllAtBaseline=true (Literal-\u003ESetVariable), then FlowForEach over the commander\u0027s UnitRoster (curated UnitRosterOps.Count/Subordinate) whose body reads each subordinate\u0027s NavigationStatus.Result via GetComponent(Target=CurrentItem), compares it against Literal(NavigationResult.Arrived) via the native Compare node (Operator=Equal, IrOp_Compare emits the infix \u0027==\u0027 inline), and BRANCHES on the Compare.Result: on \u0027not arrived\u0027 (Branch.False) it sets AllAtBaseline=false; on \u0027arrived\u0027 (Branch.True, unwired) nothing -- i.e. the AND-reduce \u0060if (!(nav.Result == NavigationResult.Arrived)) AllAtBaseline=false;\u0060 emitted as a nested inline if/else INSIDE the for-loop (P1b), not a BFS block split. After the loop, GetVariable(AllAtBaseline)-\u003EBranch returns Success/Failure. Proves in-body branch lowering (IrOp_If) AND the native Compare node end-to-end through the real netstandard2.0 generator. GAP-12: the enum-equality check is now fully visual (native Compare node) -- the former HillAssault2NavOps.IsArrived stopgap helper has been retired (deleted). Does not modify the C# oracle (HillAttackCommanderNodes.Condition_AreAllAtBaseline).",
    "Category": null,
    "Recipe": null
  }
